  "content": {
    "id": "p16-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Find the remainder when $P(x)=27x^3-9x+3$ is divided by:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p16-q2a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$21$",
          "worked": "By the remainder theorem, the remainder is $P(1)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=27(1)^3-9(1)+3\\\\P(1)&=27-9+3\\\\P(1)&=21\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q2b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x+2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-195$",
          "worked": "By the remainder theorem, the remainder is $P(-2)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(-2)&=27(-2)^3-9(-2)+3\\\\P(-2)&=-216+18+3\\\\P(-2)&=-195\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q2c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$3x-2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5$",
          "worked": "The divisor is zero at $x=\\frac23$, so the remainder is $P\\left(\\frac23\\right)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P\\left(\\frac23\\right)&=27\\left(\\frac23\\right)^3-9\\left(\\frac23\\right)+3\\\\P\\left(\\frac23\\right)&=27\\left(\\frac8{27}\\right)-6+3\\\\P\\left(\\frac23\\right)&=8-6+3\\\\P\\left(\\frac23\\right)&=5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      }
    ]
  },
